WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:03.730
All right!

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:06.360
Not too bad, if I do say so myself.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.980
But, it’s really surprising.

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:11.530
While at the Royal Palace,
I just happened to pick this up

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:15.540
because it looked so very strange and it seemed like it might be good for your stamina...

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.990
That was a great decision.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.330
How nice for you, Kawachi.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:22.790
Things seem to be going well.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:27.880
The only thing I have going for me is that I have to think up a bread from scratch.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:32.800
Can’t be helped since you just have to
improve on your masterpiece, <i>Japan</i> #51.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:35.680
It might be okay to just leave it that way, you know...

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:39.680
At that time, because Sophie scared us
so much, I also panicked a little, but...

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.430
I can’t imagine that those
three-tiered weirdos are strong.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.660
That is inexcusable,
Japanese representative.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.460
Wh... Where did you get in from?!

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:57.790
In the end, we are last year’s champions.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:00.580
We’re not so weak as to lose to a baldy like you.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:03.050
Baldy.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.180
What’s with that mask?!

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.710
Since I was shut up in my room the past four days,

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.920
I went for a walk in the city for some air.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.420
These were being given out.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.630
So I kinda just got one.

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:18.140
Being given out?!

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:19.100
Yeah.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.230
The locals seem to be fired up about cheering them on.

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:23.980
On the day of the match,

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:28.150
I bet a large number of people will
come to cheer them wearing these.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:31.910
A large number of people... wearing these...?

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.570
Kayser! Kayser!

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:37.950
Gross!

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:42.830
Monaco is “home” to the French
representatives and “away” for us.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:49.130
But, we must train our hearts to be
able to stand up to that kind of pressure.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:50.510
You’re right.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:53.920
If we shake in our shoes over the audience, we can’t possibly win.

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.050
What’s wrong, Azuma?

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.140
You don’t seem to be into this.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:01:59.430
Yeah...

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:01.970
Actually, he’s...

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.350
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.230
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:10.530
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.870
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:19.160
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:22.710
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:56.850
Curiouser and curiouser!!

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:58.440
The truth about the Kaysers!

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:02.020
I see...

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:06.510
You’re worried because you can’t come up with a way to improve on <i>Japan</i> #51.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:13.110
I told him that if he’s all that confident
in it, there’s no need to improve on it.

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:13.990
Azuma...

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:17.160
it’s easy to be lazy like Baldy here.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:21.340
But, a baker must always work to bake bread

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:25.610
by placing himself in the shoes of his customers.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:27.780
Otherwise, he can’t make something truly splendid.

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:33.080
You said that you’ve made a sports bread in the past.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:36.260
But it’s not like you made it for F1 racers.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:39.670
If you were to truly put yourself in their place and think...

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:40.800
Even if Baldy here can’t do it,

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:45.550
I think that a path would open up for a genius like you.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.770
I see!

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:50.020
Thank you, Suwabara.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:58.020
F1 racers, huh?

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:03.860
In this match, the level of each bread within the team is also going to be judged.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:05.070
In other words,

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:09.530
this is another chance to make
clear which one of us is better.

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:13.080
Come at me with a perfect <i>Japan</i>, Azuma!

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.790
I will show you that I can surpass it...

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:19.040
with my new <i>Lupan</i> #6!

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.500
This is a pain...

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.890
I couldn’t come up with anything in the end.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:30.140
I understand what Suwabara is trying to say, but...

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:33.100
Even if you ask me to put
myself in the place of an F1 racer...

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:36.100
I’ve never been driven at those kinds of high speeds.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.560
I mean,

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:42.610
when they’re driving so fast, can they even see anything around them?

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.370
O-Oh yeah! That’s it!

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:51.710
Kawachi, wake up.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.670
Come on, wake up.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:57.540
Wh-What is it?

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:00.050
The alarm hasn’t gone off yet.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.590
A little more...

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.340
Sophie!

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.300
Wh-wha-wha?!

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.760
My morning kiss...

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:10.430
Kiss...

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:12.600
K-Kiss?

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:18.070
Big kiss...

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:22.060
Kawachi! Whatever are you thinking?!

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:23.530
Let go of me, Kawachi!

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:26.780
Azuma!

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:27.660
I should be the one screaming!
Azuma!

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:28.780
I should be the one screaming!

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:31.780
What? You’re going to the Royal Palace again?

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:34.830
Yeah, I need some ingredients.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.290
I may be a little late, so take care of things.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:40.550
L-Late?! Hey, Azuma!

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:45.460
So, that’s how it is.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.750
Azuma went off to the Royal Palace.

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:49.630
This is worrisome.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:52.810
It takes quite a while to
walk here from the Royal Palace.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:55.140
I wonder if Kazuma will make it in time.

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:01.690
What is it? Why are you staring at my face?

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:03.780
I-Is there something on it?

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:05.980
No...

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:08.190
Yeah, Azuma really is troublesome.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:12.910
Really. His tardiness is in the
heavyweight class of being incurable.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:16.710
Looks like Azuma has come up with something.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:20.960
Oh well, there’s no sense in talking about it now.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:25.970
No need to worry. The two of us are enough to take on the three-tiered weirdos.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:28.460
Either way...

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:33.260
I mean, he said that he doesn’t use his mouth or legs as they are unnecessary for baking bread.

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:36.550
But he doesn’t even use his
hands, which are necessary, right?

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:37.720
That’s...

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:40.680
In that case, isn’t he just lazy?

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:42.680
I couldn’t possibly lose to someone like that...

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:43.280
That is inexcusable, Japanese representative.
I couldn’t possibly lose to someone like that...

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:46.400
That is inexcusable, Japanese representative.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:51.360
After all, we are last year’s champions.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:55.740
Calling us lazy or weirdos... is...

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:59.250
Don’t speak anymore, you disgrace.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:03.500
The oldest son spoke!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:04.920
It h-h-h-hurts!

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.330
Brother!

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:07.880
Don’t strangle me.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.880
I’ll stay in the back quietly.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:11.510
Forgive me!

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:13.010
Wh-What’s happening?

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.770
Th... The third son went around to the back.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.810
No. He ran away to the back?

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:27.610
And... he seems to be out of breath.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:32.190
You called me lazy, right?

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:34.990
No, no. Of course not.

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:39.200
I couldn’t possibly call Kayser-sama something like that.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.700
K-Kayser-sama?!

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.700
You’re a despicable baldy.

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:45.330
No, I don’t mean to blame you.

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:47.790
While I did it to help my brothers grow...

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:51.500
I did not lend a hand at all
until the semifinals.

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:54.300
So, it cannot be helped if I’m called lazy.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.220
No need to be so modest.

00:08:56.680 --> 00:09:00.680
But, contrary to what you said,
it’s not like I wasn’t using my hands.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:02.010
Huh?

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:02.930
It’s coming!

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:05.640
Let me show you.

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:07.940
Our true form underneath this mantle.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:10.690
Bob!

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:11.610
Yes Sir!

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.950
Wh... What is this?!

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:21.790
H-How in the world...!

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:24.200
This is it.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.790
This is the secret of the Kaysers’ strength.

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:30.170
Impossible!

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:32.790
Why is it that once the mantle was raised...

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:34.800
The first body parts we saw were...

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:37.010
his hands?!

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:39.010
Wh-Whose hands are those?!

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:42.520
Bob’s hands are raising the mantle, so...

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:43.900
They must be Edward’s!

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:46.810
No, those are the oldest son Gran’s hands!

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:50.230
Impossible!

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:54.070
If that were the case, just Gran’s
arms alone would be about 3 meters long!

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:57.580
The exact value is 2 meters and 72 centimeters.

00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:59.990
Y-You’re kidding?!

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:03.030
In order to move just one step
closer to my father, Alexis Kayser,

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:06.200
the great founder of our bakery...

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.210
Ever since childhood,

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:13.090
I have reinforced the strength in my
arms, which is most important to a baker.

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:18.680
Of course, in the beginning, I couldn’t even move them.

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:24.220
But a human being’s passion is a terrifying thing.

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:30.600
As time passed, I grew to be able to move them little by little.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:32.200
And, before I realized it...

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:39.620
As a result of the training, my
arms had grown extremely long.

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:44.290
Well, see you at the semifinals then.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:46.660
Wait!

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:49.370
You plan to run away with a
half-assed explanation like that?!

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:59.340
Well, I’m kind of wondering how
exactly you’re stacked inside, but...

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:02.180
Uh... Nothing.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:03.760
You want to see?

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:05.980
Very much.

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:07.780
Very well.

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:13.020
Wh... Wh... What is this?!

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:26.200
Wh... Wh... What is this?!

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:30.700
I-I don’t believe it.

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:34.170
The oldest son is supporting both
their bodies with just his hands?

00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:38.550
But, you can’t use your hands when you’re like that!

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:40.170
So how do you make bread then?

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:42.720
Bob, final formation.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:43.680
Yes Sir!

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:51.850
Th... This is like...

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:54.350
Chiron, from Greek mythology!

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:56.860
Also known as a centaur!

00:11:57.230 --> 00:12:01.320
What’s more surprising than that
formation is the sheer width of his arms!

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.360
If looks like it’s twice that of Bob’s.

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:07.660
Sorry for shocking you, Japanese representatives.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:10.370
In addition to the Solar Hands that I was born with,

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:16.590
I added on two times the amount of
muscle needed for a normal Solar Gauntlet.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:16.630
Solar Hands Gigantous
I added on two times the amount of
muscle needed for a normal Solar Gauntlet.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:19.380
These hands are the Solar Hands Gigantous.
Solar Hands Gigantous

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:21.880
Solar Hands Gigantous?!

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.130
And in addition...

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:28.850
That motion of his fingers!

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:30.140
The Goddess’s Hands.

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:31.350
La Main De Deesse.

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:35.310
Suwabara, why don’t you
counterattack with your La Main De Deesse?

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:36.350
It’s impossible.

00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:39.360
That’s no longer the
movement of a human being’s hands.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.940
As a result of using my hands as legs,

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:44.070
the joints in my fingers have become supple.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:46.030
If necessary, I can move

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:51.540
each and every one of my fingers around separately, at a full 360°.

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:54.380
La Main De Deesse Ultima.

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:56.830
La Main De Deesse Ultima!

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:58.170
This is it.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:01.590
This is the proof of the Kaysers being #1 in the world.

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:05.010
There doesn’t exist a baker in this
world who can defeat the Kaysers.

00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:10.010
Wait, wait.

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:11.640
Sorry to interrupt your fun, but...

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:14.720
The starting time for the match has passed long ago.

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:15.520
What?

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:19.730
At this rate, the audience will get tired of waiting and riot.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:26.240
See you at the match hall then.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.000
That match is about to start.

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:31.740
Azuma, what are you doing?

00:13:31.740 --> 00:13:33.170
Come quickly, will you?!

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:44.380
As expected of the semifinals of a world tournament.

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:47.510
The number of people in the audience is amazing.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:49.010
Y... Yeah.

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:51.220
And, as expected, they’re here.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:53.810
The number of people in masks is large.

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:56.220
We’re the away team here.

00:13:56.220 --> 00:13:58.440
To top it off, our opponent is that monster.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:00.230
And Azuma is late.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:02.230
The worst possible circumstances, aren’t they?

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:04.230
Late, huh?

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:07.280
The time limit on this match is 150 minutes.

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:10.950
So, if he makes the bread within that time, there is no problem.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:13.960
Should he go even one minute
over that, he will be disqualified.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:20.420
Leaving aside specially made breads, a
normal bread will need at least 90 minutes.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:23.130
Azuma may no longer make it in time.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:25.090
Can’t be helped.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:29.720
Azuma, I wanted to settle
things with you one more time.

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:31.090
It’s a shame.

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:32.590
Listen up, Kawachi.

00:14:32.590 --> 00:14:34.200
Even Kayser is the son of a human being.

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:36.430
Should we give it everything we’ve got,

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:38.230
while you may lose,

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:39.100
I’ll win!

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:40.390
That’s right.

00:14:40.390 --> 00:14:41.650
Hey, wait!

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:44.150
Why do you always treat me like a loser?!

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:45.320
Let’s do it!

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:46.190
All right!

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:47.820
Hey, don’t expect me to answer to something like that!

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:50.950
I think that you’ll have a
hard time without Azuma, but...

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:53.080
good luck to the both of you.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:56.040
All right then everyone...
Sorry for the wait.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:15:00.080
We’re starting the semifinals
of the Second Monaco Cup.

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:01.510
Begin!

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:06.420
Azuma being late was a
miscalculation on our part, but...

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:08.590
Even I have a secret weapon this time!

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:10.840
This is it!

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:15.220
What is that?

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:16.970
It’s all craggy and gross.

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:19.680
Well, it’s not something that you’d be familiar with.

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:22.600
Whatever. Stop showing off and tell me.

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:24.190
Oh well...

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:24.600
That is...

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:25.490
Aren’t those corn barnacles?
That is...

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:26.610
Aren’t those corn barnacles?

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:28.150
Corn barnacles?

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:29.820
Th... That’s right.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:31.360
Corn barnacles?

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:32.070
What is that?

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:36.290
Guests from Italy must know about it.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:40.120
Corn barnacles are found
sticking to rocks on ocean beaches.

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:42.870
Despite their bad appearance,

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:46.840
they are considered high-class food in Italy and Japan.

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:51.840
They have been so popular
in recent years that in Japan...

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:57.060
umm... about 1 kilogram
would sell for 5000 or 10,000 yen.

00:15:57.550 --> 00:16:00.220
I... I didn’t know that.

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:04.020
But... my ability to judge ingredients is impressive.

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:07.070
This really was an amazing ingredient.

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:11.780
Just boiling it gives a rich taste,

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:14.080
which does not lose to any other ingredient I know.

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:18.580
And, they have a strong life-force,
allowing them to stick to rocks.

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:23.710
I’m sure that they are rich in
nutrients essential to a sportsman.

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:26.080
Prepare yourself, Gran Kayser.

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:29.890
I’m going to win this match!

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:33.050
Wh... What is that?

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:36.060
Something is shining on Kayser’s table.

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:38.220
What in the world is that?!

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:40.140
What is that powder?

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:42.560
It’s shining like a jewel.

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:44.180
There’s no mistaking it. That’s p...

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:44.730
That’s pearl powder!
There’s no mistaking it. That’s p...

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:46.390
That’s pearl powder!

00:16:46.390 --> 00:16:48.610
Pearl powder?!

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:50.070
Y-Yeah.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:50.990
Pearl.

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:56.610
Pearl powder is a food of beauty that was once loved by Youkihi.

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:59.030
Pearls have a larger number of antioxidants in them,

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:02.080
which are supposed to be
effective in making you beautiful.

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:03.660
What’s that?

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:04.830
For a sportsman?

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:07.620
Beauty has nothing to do with it!

00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:09.630
No, no, no, no, no. That’s not true.

00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:15.180
Antioxidants don’t just affect your beauty.

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:17.430
You know that a large amount

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:22.640
of active oxygen collects in your
body when you do sports, right?

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:27.350
In order to inactivate them, it’s necessary to eat foods that contain antioxidants.

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:28.400
In other words,

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:32.860
Pearl powder is one of the best
ingredients you can use in a sports bread.

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:35.070
F-For real?!

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:39.280
Moreover, he’s not using any old pearl powder.

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:42.700
It’s the purest kind of Kan Kyuu Mo Powder from Jiangsu in the Tai mountain area.

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:43.250
Pearl Powder
It’s the purest kind of Kan Kyuu Mo Powder from Jiangsu in the Tai mountain area.

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:44.580
Pearl Powder

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.660
It’s said that compared to regular pearl powder,

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:50.960
it has more than three times the capability of absorbing effective ingredients.

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:52.590
It not only helps the body
absorb antioxidants present in pearls,

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:56.920
it also has an abundance of
natural amino acids and calcium.

00:17:56.920 --> 00:17:59.590
It’s the ultimate fine powder.

00:17:59.590 --> 00:18:00.470
Did you see that?!

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:01.850
That’s the Kaysers for you!

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:03.600
A country like Japan is no match for you!

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:08.310
In addition to strong Solar Hands and a La Main De Deesse...

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:11.400
he’s also perfect in his choice of ingredients.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:12.740
Gran Kayser...

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:17.070
Is it true that people like us
can’t match up to him?

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:21.320
I have yet another secret hidden up my sleeve and so...

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:24.160
To think that something like
this has already shocked them...

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:27.040
I’m disappointed,
Japanese representatives.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:32.790
I guess other than that boy, this
team was made up of small fry.

00:18:33.790 --> 00:18:37.550
Kawachi, why are you getting
agitated over some stupid pearls?

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:39.300
Tha... That’s true, but...

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:40.800
Suwabara!

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:44.020
What’s with his dough?!

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:47.470
What’s with Kai’s dough?

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:49.560
It’s completely red!

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:51.280
Why don’t you just ask Pierrot?

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:54.730
The reason as to why his dough is red?

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:56.320
That’s fresh blood from the snapping turtle.

00:18:56.980 --> 00:19:00.610
You mixed that with red wine and kneaded it into the bread, right?

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:04.620
This may also be something that the
French may not be familiar with, but...

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:08.330
it’s a famous food item in Japan.

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:12.750
In addition to being rich in gelatin,
which has an abundance of animal protein,

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:16.340
this fresh blood can also act as a
central nervous system stimulant.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:19.840
Just drinking it will make your whole body go really hot.

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:24.140
In addition, the red wine that is mixed in with the blood

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:29.060
has anthocyanin, which is a
great nutrient for your eyes.

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:35.190
In other words, for F1 racers who are straining their eyes going at speeds of 300km/hour,

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:39.580
an essential ingredient has been kneaded in.

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:42.450
As expected of a world-level clown.

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:43.740
You’re well informed.

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:45.740
That’s exactly how it is.

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:50.290
This is the power of my new Crimson <i>Lupan</i> #6.

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:53.540
Japan is pretty good, too.

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:56.130
Even Kayser may not be able to let down his guard.

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:00.670
Take that, Gran Kayser!

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:02.470
This is Japan’s true strength.

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:03.800
Do you understand now?

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:06.050
Don’t show off like you’ve made it.

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:08.020
That doesn’t matter at this point.

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:13.610
More than pearls, it’s giant nycin you want, giant nycin.

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:15.560
That’s “anthocyanin.”

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:19.530
My dough has anthocyanin in it as well.

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:21.070
W-What was that?!

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:27.530
Blue?!

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:32.620
Kayser’s dough is a deep blue.

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:34.290
How did he get that color?!

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:36.500
Blueberries!

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:38.090
Correct!

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:44.630
Blueberries are fruit with a large amount of anthocyanin in them.

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:49.680
These were crushed and kneaded into
the dough with a special yogurt sauce.

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:53.230
In addition to anthocyanin,
due to mixing in the yogurt,

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:59.650
animal protein, vitamins, and
nutrients like calcium are mixed in.

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:01.440
Just as expected of Kayser!

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:03.650
Crush those damn Japanese!

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:09.200
But, the results of the match
cannot be known until the bread is done.

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:11.370
My Crimson <i>Lupan</i> #6 is...

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:15.870
I’m sorry, but you bread is already... over with.

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:16.880
What?!

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:20.370
Your bread has a fatal flaw.

00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:22.130
Wh-What was that?!

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:25.050
It is a crime to present that
unsuitable bread in this place.

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:27.380
To think that you want to
challenge me with that bread...

00:21:27.380 --> 00:21:28.890
You’re three centuries too early!

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:30.390
Wha...

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:32.100
Wh-What was that?!

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:34.850
Based on what are you...?

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:36.350
To not even know that...

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:39.610
You really were not a match for me.

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:42.110
Im... Impossible.

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:48.490
I don’t think that he’s the kind of guy to bluff about this.

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:50.030
He’s serious.

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:51.990
He’s seriously convinced about this.

00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:54.040
This isn’t good...

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:56.870
I was optimistic for a moment that Suwabara would win for sure.

00:21:56.870 --> 00:21:59.500
But Kayser had a similar trick up his sleeve, too.

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:05.010
On top of that, if there’s a flaw
to Suwabara’s bread, as he says...

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:07.760
we have no way to win...

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:11.980
Our last hope is for Azuma to make it in on time, but...

00:22:13.680 --> 00:22:16.730
Only 90 minutes left.

00:22:17.230 --> 00:22:19.850
Only 90 minutes?! Oh no!

00:22:19.850 --> 00:22:22.980
We no longer have enough time to finish the bread.

00:22:29.400 --> 00:22:31.450
We’re finished!

00:22:31.450 --> 00:22:33.840
We’re in the most dire of dire straits!

00:24:05.710 --> 00:24:06.960
Kai’s red bread.

00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:08.300
Kayser’s blue bread.

00:24:08.300 --> 00:24:09.800
And Azuma’s black bread.

00:24:09.800 --> 00:24:12.760
I’m all hyper since all of them
got full points for nutritional value.

00:24:15.220 --> 00:24:16.890
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.890 --> 00:24:18.930
Lots of nutrients!! The Sports Bread Showdown!

00:24:18.930 --> 00:24:19.980
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.470 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.010 --> 00:24:24.140
Snapping turtles!

00:24:24.140 --> 00:24:27.110
The hexadecenoic acid and eicosapentanoic acid in snapping turtles

00:24:27.110 --> 00:24:29.110
help get rid of bad cholesterol.

00:24:29.110 --> 00:24:31.750
In addition to stimulating the CNS, it helps in revitalization.

00:24:31.750 --> 00:24:34.290
Oh?!
